    "title": "Bubble Sort — Student Marks",
    "gist": "Sort student marks in ascending order using Bubble Sort.",
    "description": "Question: Sort the marks [75, 42, 90, 61, 55] in ascending order using Bubble Sort. Compare adjacent elements and swap them when they are out of order. Data structures: Integer array and temporary variable. Assumed time complexity: O(n²). Auxiliary space complexity: O(1). Expected output: [42, 55, 61, 75, 90]. Learning goals: Array traversal, nested loops, comparisons, swapping, and in-place sorting.",
    "code": "class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        int[] marks = {75, 42, 90, 61, 55};\n        visual(marks, \"array\");\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < marks.length - 1; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < marks.length - i - 1; j++) {\n                if (marks[j] > marks[j + 1]) {\n                    point(marks, j, \"orange\");\n                    point(marks, j + 1, \"blue\");\n                    int temp = marks[j];\n                    marks[j] = marks[j + 1];\n                    marks[j + 1] = temp;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(java.util.Arrays.toString(marks));\n    }\n\n    static void visual(Object object, String type) {}\n    static void point(Object object, String color) {}\n    static void point(Object array, int index, String color) {}\n    static void point(Object matrix, int row, int column, String color) {}\n}",
